    text: "Eight. Good weight, clean ends. ... And you saw it. Split top to root, and green on the west side, still. Fifty years like that. That is why the rule is eight and never the ninth: a thing can be that far gone and still be working. Take the hatchet. Iron. It will hold an edge in the deep stand.",
